&lt;p&gt;LaunchDarkly is hiring a VP of Partnerships &amp;amp; Alliances to lead and scale partnerships as a measurable growth engine across GSIs and SIs, cloud, VARs, and technology partners. This executive will own the global partner strategy and build the programs, services, and co-sell motions that expand customer reach and accelerate revenue across LaunchDarkly’s product portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact executive leadership role for a strategic, hands-on operator who can build and lead a high-performing organization, develop executive partner relationships, and make partnerships part of the core go-to-market motion. As a member of the extended Revenue leadership team, the VP of Partnerships will work closely with Sales, Professional Services, Customer Success, Product, Marketing, Finance, Legal, Enablement, and Revenue Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an exciting opportunity to play a leading role in scaling partner-led adoption of LaunchDarkly’s AI Runtime Control, creating differentiated joint value and accelerating growth through strategic alliances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the global partnerships strategy, translating company and Revenue priorities into a 2–4 year roadmap and annual plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead the Partnerships organization, establishing the operating model, talent strategy, and accountability needed to scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct the partnerships budget and investment priorities, driving measurable contribution to partner-sourced pipeline, partner-influenced revenue, and growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design the global partner program architecture across Services and SI, Resell and VAR, Cloud, and Technology partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align priority partners to LaunchDarkly’s go-to-market strategy through account mapping, co-selling, co-marketing, and expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish operating rhythms and executive reporting for partner-sourced and partner-influenced pipeline, revenue, forecasting, and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the strategy and rollout of a scalable PRM ecosystem integrated with Salesforce, including deal registration, attribution, partner workflows, and data integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop repeatable GSI and SI service offerings with Professional Services, Customer Success, and Product across implementation, modernization, AI, and DevOps transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand referral, co-delivery, subcontracting, and marketplace motions once the underlying economics, delivery models, and customer value are proven.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the partner activation and enablement engine across onboarding, certifications, playbooks, demos, and seller workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate partnerships into account planning, forecast reviews, QBRs, strategic deals, and the Revenue operating cadence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape joint solutions, integrations, and priority use cases with Product and Solutions Architecture across DevOps, AI, observability, and experimentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Partnerships in Revenue and company-wide planning, operating reviews, and strategic initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Typically requires 15+ years of experience in B2B SaaS partnerships, alliances, channel, or related revenue roles, including at least 7 years leading partnerships leaders, managers, or directors and significant experience with Services, SI, or GSI partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success leading global partner strategies, building or relaunching partner programs across distinct partner motions, and owning partner-sourced and partner-influenced pipeline and revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading and scaling a Partnerships organization with multiple partner segments, programs, and cross-functional dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with PRM, Salesforce, deal registration, partner data, attribution, and revenue reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating GSI and SI services and scaling co-delivery, referral, subcontracting, or marketplace motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building co-sell programs with cloud, hyperscaler, technology, or data platform partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional leadership, executive presence, and commercial judgment across Sales, Product, Professional Services, Finance, Marketing, Legal, and Revenue Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in DevOps, developer tools, observability, AI and ML, or related technology ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strategic, data-informed approach to prioritization, budget allocation, and operating cadence, with the ability to build structure in a fast-changing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting corporate development initiatives involving strategic partners and influencing company-level decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Target pay ranges based on Geographic Zones* for Level E1:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Zone 1: &lt;em&gt;San Francisco/Bay Area or NYC Metropolitan Area, Boston, Seattle&lt;/em&gt; - &lt;em&gt;$&lt;span class=&quot;collapsed-field-text&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;37&lt;/em&gt;8,000 - $520,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;**&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Zone 2:&lt;em&gt; Irvine, LA, Monterey, Santa Barbara, Santa Rosa, Austin, Portland, Philadelphia, Chicago - $&lt;span class=&quot;collapsed-field-text&quot;&gt;340,000 - $468,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;**&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Zone 3: &lt;em&gt;All other US locations - $&lt;span class=&quot;collapsed-field-text&quot;&gt;321,000 - $442,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;**&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;LaunchDarkly operates from a place of high trust and transparency; we are happy to state the pay range for our open roles to best align with your needs. Exact compensation may vary based on skills, experience, and location.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
