&lt;li&gt;Location: Remote-first (Argentina)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Permanent, full-time employee (this is not a contractor position)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Application Information:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Application deadline: applications accepted on an ongoing basis until position is closed and filled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This posting is for an existing vacancy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reporting to the Senior Engineering Manager, Developer Productivity&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer, Developer Productivity&lt;/strong&gt;, you&#39;ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build the Nest.js service scaffolding that lets product teams stand up new backend services in our next-generation monorepo&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement paved paths, generators, and the platform primitives that make a new service work on day one rather than after a week of wiring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the seams that let new services run independently of our existing monolith.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the deployment story for services and web applications on Cloudflare, and the interoperability with our existing AWS and Kubernetes estate managed through Pulumi and Argo CD.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead migrations of substantial codebases into the monorepo and turn each one into a repeatable recipe rather than a bespoke effort.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with product teams as platform customers, treating their adoption as the measure of success and their friction as your backlog.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the leverage of the whole team by encoding what you learn into tooling, generators and agent-assisted workflows, so the next migration costs less than the last.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in engineering citizenship activities such as co-authoring engineering blogs, strengthening our hiring processes, and leading internal hackathon teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Requirements:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA/BS Degree or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years building and operating backend services in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience in backend service design &amp;nbsp;defining service boundaries, contracts and data ownership, not only implementing within them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business-level fluency to read, write and speak in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll thrive as a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer, Developer Productivity,&lt;/strong&gt; if you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked inside a large, heavily-coupled codebase and found the seams: extracting or bypassing functionality incrementally, behind behaviour-preserving contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are fluent in TypeScript and Node, and comfortable with edge runtimes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have hands-on experience with monorepo tooling at scale (Nx, Turborepo or similar) and understand why build-graph correctness is a product concern rather than a config detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treat migration work as engineering rather than chores: you budget for the parts that fail silently, verify generated output rather than trusting a green build, and know that bug-for-bug translation&amp;nbsp;beats improvement when the goal is proving nothing changed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy being a platform engineer with real customers — partnering with product teams, adapting the platform to how they actually work rather than requiring them to change, and measuring yourself on their adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable working across cloud boundaries, with a considered view on where a workload belongs and what crossing between clouds costs in latency and spend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate decisions in writing well enough that someone can pick up your work from the ticket — and are willing to say plainly when the fast answer and the right answer diverge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay curious and open to growth — demonstrating a proactive embrace of AI, and actively building and applying fluency in emerging technologies to elevate how we work, drive faster outcomes, and expand collective impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Core Behaviors:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build lasting customer trust.&lt;/strong&gt; We build trust by taking action that puts customer trust first.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Win together.&lt;/strong&gt; We play to win, and we win as one team. Success at Webflow isn&#39;t a solo act.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reinvent ourselves. &lt;/strong&gt;We don&#39;t just improve what exists, we imagine what&#39;s possible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own it all the way. &lt;/strong&gt;We move fast because the moment demands it, and we hold ourselves accountable to deliver outcomes — for each other, and for customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership in what you help build.&lt;/strong&gt; Every permanent Webflower receives equity (RSUs) in our growing, privately held company.&lt;/li&gt;
