application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scopely &lt;/strong&gt;is seeking a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Director, Cloud Governance&lt;/strong&gt; to lead efforts in establishing and enforcing standards, policies, and guardrails across Scopely’s multi-cloud environment.&amp;nbsp; This is a remote opportunity for individuals in Canada or the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Director, Cloud Governance&lt;/strong&gt; you will play a pivotal leadership role in defining and executing the Scopely’s Cloud Governance strategy. This team will define, implement, and enforce the policies and controls that govern how cloud infrastructure is used across a decentralized organization of game, platform, and product teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is critical to bringing structure, consistency, and guardrails to Scopely’s cloud footprint, and will be key in modernizing our overall governance posture. As a central leader, you will drive alignment across highly autonomous teams and translate governance into practical, adoptable solutions while balancing control and development velocity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a foundational leadership role; you will establish governance from the ground up, introduce scalable and enforceable controls, and drive adoption and buy-in across various teams, stakeholders, and senior leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Build &amp;amp; Lead Cloud Governance&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead a Cloud Governance team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the operating model for how governance partners with game teams, security, and FinOps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear ownership and enforcement mechanisms for cloud policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define &amp;amp; Enforce Cloud Guardrails&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement enforceable controls across AWS and GCP, including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS Organizations, Service Control Policies (SCPs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GCP Organization Policies and IAM constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish guardrails around:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resource provisioning and service usage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Region restrictions and data residency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identity and access management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network architecture and environment isolation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the mandate to enforce policies, including the ability to restrict or block non-compliant usage&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standardize Cloud Structure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and implement standards for:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS account structure and GCP project/folder hierarchy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Environment segmentation (prod, staging, dev)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Naming conventions and resource organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring consistency across a fragmented, multi-team cloud footprint&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tagging &amp;amp; Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and enforce tagging standards in partnership with FinOps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all resources are attributable (ownership, environment, cost center)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable downstream cost allocation and operational visibility&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Stakeholder Partnership&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with FinOps on cost allocation and optimization levers (budgets, quotas, usage controls)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Security to align governance with security and compliance requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with game teams to safely roll out and drive adoption of policies and standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;AI-Forward Governance &amp;amp; Automation&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute an AI-native vision for cloud governance, transforming the function into an intelligent, policy-driven operating model powered by autonomous and agentic systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the organization’s strategy for governance autonomy, defining where fully autonomous operations, human-on-the-loop oversight, and human-in-the-loop approvals are appropriate based on risk, business impact, and compliance requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and drive agentic governance capabilities that continuously monitor cloud environments, detect risk, and autonomously remediate anomalies at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across engineering, data, and security, and platform teams to embed responsible AI governance into cloud platforms, establishing guardrails for AI adoption, autonomous decision-making, and auditability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in cloud infrastructure, platform engineering, or SRE&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5+ years leading teams in complex, multi-team environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in decentralized or federated engineering organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record implementing cloud governance and enforcement at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing or influencing environments with $50M+ cloud spend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on experience with AWS and/or GCP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with Infrastructure as Code (e.g., Terraform)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with policy-as-code and governance tooling (e.g., OPA, Sentinel, AWS Config)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of cloud networking, identity, and multi-account design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For candidates in CA, CO, NJ, NY, and WA, the annual salary range is provided below. In addition to base pay, employees may be eligible for equity, bonuses, and a comprehensive benefits package, including healthcare benefits, retirement benefits, pet insurance, paid holidays, paid Scopely free days, and unlimited paid time off. Base pay offered may vary depending on job-related knowledge, skills, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;CA, CO, NJ, NY, and WA Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$175,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$210,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Scopely&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a leading video game and global interactive entertainment company, home to many of the world’s most beloved and enduring experiences, including two of the most successful mobile games of all-time “MONOPOLY GO!” and “Pokémon GO,” along with “Stumble Guys,” “Star Trek™ Fleet Command,” “MARVEL Strike Force,” “WWE Champions,” the Scrabble® franchise, “Yahtzee® With Buddies,” and many others. Across mobile, web, PC, and console, Scopely creates, develops, publishes, and live-operates one of the most diversified and award-winning portfolios in the games industry — bringing hundreds of millions of players together through a shared love of play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2011, Scopely is powered by its exceptional team — including thousands of world-class gamemakers around the globe, a distinctive tenet-driven culture, and its proprietary technology platform, Playgami. Together, these strengths have fueled Scopely’s position as the #1 mobile games company in the U.S. and #2 globally, generating more than $10 billion in lifetime revenue. Whether building global sensations like “MONOPOLY GO!” from the ground up, or expanding through strategic acquisitions, including the FoxNext, GSN, and Scopely Explore games businesses — Scopely consistently delivers experiences players love today and return to for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized multiple times as one of the &quot;100 Most Influential Companies in the World&quot; by TIME magazine and one of Fast Company&#39;s &quot;World&#39;s Most Innovative Companies&quot; and “Best Workplaces for Innovators,” Scopely believes that video games can be a force for good — creating meaningful connections, vibrant communities, and making life better through play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely has global operations and partners across four continents in more than a dozen countries worldwide. For more information, visit: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.scopely.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Candidates: Scopely will never request payment or financial information during the application or hiring process. Please apply only through our official &lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt; and verify that all Talent Partner communications come from an email address ending in @&lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;scopely.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Should you have any questions or encounter any fraudulent requests/emails/websites, please immediately contact recruiting@scopely.com. Our job applicant privacy policies are available here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/job-applicant-privacy-notice-for-ca-residents&quot;&gt;California Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/eea-and-uk-job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;EEA/UK Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employment at Scopely is based solely on a person&#39;s merit and qualifications. Scopely does not discriminate against any employee or applicant because of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), or any other basis protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;","departments":[{"id":4033440008,"name":"Operations","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4036521008,"name":"Remote - Ontario","location":null,"child_ids":[],"parent_id":4029780008}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/scopely/jobs/5414563008?gh_jid=5414563008","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":4543297008,"location":{"name":"US - Culver City, California, United States"},"metadata":[{"id":4974618008,"name":"Worker Type","value":"Employee","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6354091008,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full Time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6354150008,"name":"Referral Bonus Payout Type","value":"Standard","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6710077008,"name":"Work Arrangement","value":["Hybrid"],"value_type":"multi_select"},{"id":6752710008,"name":"Location","value":["United States"],"value_type":"multi_select"},{"id":6755132008,"name":"Category","value":["Corporate"],"value_type":"multi_select"}],"id":5414563008,"updated_at":"2026-09-02T20:17:13-04:00","requisition_id":"JR106685","title":"Director, Legal Operations","company_name":"Scopely","first_published":"2026-09-02T20:17:13-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;Scopely is seeking&amp;nbsp; a &lt;strong&gt;Director, Legal Operations&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Legal team. This role will lead the Legal Operations function and establish the strategy, operating model, technology roadmap, governance framework, and performance infrastructure for a global, high-growth Legal department.&amp;nbsp; This role will be a hybrid position in our Culver City, CA hub.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director will directly manage the Sr. Manager, Legal Operations, who owns day-to-day Ironclad CLM operations, knowledge management infrastructure, and AI-enabled legal technology implementation. The Director will provide strategic direction, prioritize the team’s roadmap, manage resources and vendors, and remain accountable for the quality, adoption, and business impact of these programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior people-leadership and functional-building role for someone who can translate Legal leadership’s priorities into scalable systems, processes, and measurable outcomes. The right candidate will combine strategic judgment, operational discipline, technical fluency, executive presence, and the ability to build trusted partnerships across Legal and the broader business . as a strategic business partner, not just a support or systems-administration function. They will be comfortable operating in ambiguity, creating structure where none exists, and leading through influence in a fast-paced global gaming company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Legal Operations Strategy &amp;amp; Functional Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with Legal leadership to define and execute a multi-year Legal Operations strategy aligned with Scopely’s business priorities and growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate Legal department priorities into an integrated roadmap covering technology, process improvement, data, knowledge management, automation, training, and organizational capability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish annual and quarterly priorities, success metrics, resource plans, and sequencing recommendations for the Legal Operations team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise Legal leadership on tradeoffs among business impact, risk, cost, speed, and available team capacity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the Legal Operations budget, oversee spend, build business cases for new investments, and manage vendor and renewal strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to standardize, automate, and simplify Legal processes across Commercial, Corporate, Employment, Product Compliance, and other Legal functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly manage, coach, and develop the Sr. Manager, Legal Operations, who owns Ironclad CLM operations, knowledge management infrastructure, and AI implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Legal Technology Strategy &amp;amp; Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the executive owner of Scopely’s Legal technology portfolio and establish a coherent architecture and investment strategy across CLM, knowledge management, matter management, e-billing, contract analytics, automation, and related tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Legal technology roadmap, including technology selection, implementation sequencing, integration priorities, system rationalization, and long-term scalability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee Ironclad CLM as a critical Legal and business system, ensuring that the Sr. Manager has the direction, resources, governance framework, and stakeholder alignment necessary to operate the platform effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish governance standards for workflow design, metadata, templates, permissions, approval logic, integrations, repository integrity, data retention, change management, and system access&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and approve significant platform changes, balancing user experience, business needs, control requirements, data integrity, and long-term maintainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with IT, Information Security, Privacy, Procurement, Finance, and external vendors on architecture, security, integrations, implementation, support, and risk management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead or oversee system migrations, data consolidation efforts, post-acquisition integrations, and other technology transformation initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge Management, Automation &amp;amp; AI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the strategic vision and operating model for Legal knowledge management, including content architecture, taxonomy, ownership, curation, searchability, version control, and access governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that Legal’s institutional knowledge is captured, structured, maintained, and made accessible in ways that support self-service, consistency, and future AI applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a portfolio of practical AI and automation use cases for Legal in partnership with Legal leadership, IT, and relevant business stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the implementation and responsible adoption of AI-enabled tools, including chatbots, knowledge-based assistants, workflow automation, contract analytics, and other emerging technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct the Sr. Manager’s hands-on execution of knowledge management and AI initiatives, including platform configuration, testing, content population, user feedback, optimization, and rollout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define success metrics for AI and automation initiatives, including adoption, response quality, time saved, reduction in repetitive inquiries, and measurable improvements to the Legal user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on legal technology and AI developments and make informed recommendations regarding opportunities, risks, and investment priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Improvement &amp;amp; Business Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a strategic partner to Legal leadership, Procurement, Finance, Information Security, IT, People, Product, and other stakeholders to improve the end-to-end process of contracting and Legal support experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish scalable intake, triage, and routing models that direct work to the appropriate Legal or business resource and minimize unnecessary attorney involvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use qualitative and quantitative data to identify recurring friction, diagnose root causes, and implement structural solutions rather than one-off fixes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Legal leadership to define and adopt practical playbooks, self-service resources, approval frameworks, and standardized workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data, Analytics &amp;amp; Performance Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a strategic partner with Commercial Legal to design and monitor metrics such as contracting cycle times, intake volumes, routing accuracy, self-service rates, workflow adoption, support trends, system reliability, automation impact, and stakeholder satisfaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a Legal Operations performance framework that measures the efficiency, quality, adoption, capacity, and business impact of Legal services and systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create executive-ready dashboards and reporting for Legal leadership, highlighting trends, risks, opportunities, and recommended actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data to support capacity planning, prioritization, investment decisions, vendor management, and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7-10+ years of experience in Legal Operations, legal technology, business operations, process transformation, consulting, or a related field, with clear progression in scope, responsibility, and organizational leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading or building a Legal Operations function within a high-growth technology, gaming, entertainment, digital media, or similarly complex global company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 3–5 years of experience managing, coaching, and developing professionals, including experience setting priorities, delegating ownership, giving feedback, and building team capability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing a Legal Operations strategy, operating model, roadmap, budget, governance framework, and performance-measurement program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience with enterprise CLM programs, including Ironclad or a comparable platform. Direct Ironclad administration experience is strongly preferred; the candidate must have sufficient technical depth to evaluate platform architecture, workflow design, data governance, integrations, controls, and adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage budgets, negotiate with vendors, assess technology investments, and measure realized value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience overseeing legal technology portfolios beyond CLM, such as knowledge management, e-billing, matter management, contract analytics, automation, compliance, or AI-enabled tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build or mature a knowledge management function and translate institutional knowledge into structured, searchable, reusable content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience evaluating, implementing, governing, or scaling AI and automation tools in a professional-services, legal, technology, or corporate environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and systems-thinking skills, with the ability to identify patterns, diagnose root causes, and design solutions that scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent executive presence and communication skills, with the ability to influence senior Legal and business leaders and translate technical or operational issues into clear business decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project and change-management skills, including the ability to lead complex initiatives across multiple teams with competing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A highly collaborative, practical, and service-oriented leadership style, with the judgment to balance user experience, business enablement, risk management, and operational discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating with significant autonomy in a fast-paced, evolving environment and the ability to create clarity, structure, and momentum amid ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading Legal Operations in a gaming, interactive entertainment, digital media, or consumer technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with Ironclad, contract analytics, legal knowledge platforms, or similar tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with post-acquisition Legal technology integrations, data migrations, or operating-model integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing outside counsel, legal vendors, e-billing, matter management, or Legal department spend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing responsible-use standards or governance frameworks for AI in a Legal or regulated environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with geographically distributed teams and supporting global Legal operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A sense of humor and a passion for mobile gaming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within the first year, the Director will have established a clear Legal Operations strategy and roadmap; created a well-functioning operating model for the Legal Operations team; enabled the Sr. Manager to own day-to-day CLM, knowledge management, and AI execution; implemented a consistent performance-reporting framework; strengthened governance across Legal technology; and delivered measurable improvements in self-service, workflow adoption, contracting efficiency, and Legal team capacity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please ensure that the résumé/CV you attach is written in English.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For candidates in CA, CO, NJ, NY, and WA, the annual salary range is provided below. In addition to base pay, employees may be eligible for equity, bonuses, and a comprehensive benefits package, including healthcare benefits, retirement benefits, pet insurance, paid holidays, paid Scopely free days, and unlimited paid time off. Base pay offered may vary depending on job-related knowledge, skills, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;CA, CO, NJ, NY, and WA Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$160,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$176,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
