&lt;p&gt;Should you have any questions or encounter any fraudulent requests/emails/websites, please immediately contact recruiting@scopely.com. Our job applicant privacy policies are available here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/job-applicant-privacy-notice-for-ca-residents&quot;&gt;California Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/eea-and-uk-job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;EEA/UK Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employment at Scopely is based solely on a person&#39;s merit and qualifications. Scopely does not discriminate against any employee or applicant because of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), or any other basis protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;","departments":[{"id":4033435008,"name":"Legal","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4036293008,"name":"Culver City","location":"Culver City, California, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4046122008}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/scopely/jobs/5400350008?gh_jid=5400350008","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":4537674008,"location":{"name":"US - United States"},"metadata":[{"id":4974618008,"name":"Worker Type","value":"Employee","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6354091008,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full Time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6354150008,"name":"Referral Bonus Payout Type","value":null,"value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6710077008,"name":"Work Arrangement","value":null,"value_type":"multi_select"},{"id":6752710008,"name":"Location","value":null,"value_type":"multi_select"},{"id":6755132008,"name":"Category","value":null,"value_type":"multi_select"}],"id":5400350008,"updated_at":"2026-09-03T13:34:23-04:00","requisition_id":"JR106556","title":"Director of Community - Unannounced Project","company_name":"Scopely","first_published":"2026-09-03T13:34:23-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a Director of Community to join an unannounced project team remotely in the US.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play, every day - whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues, or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing and innovating the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are in the development stages of one of our new unannounced projects, and are looking for passionate game makers to collaborate, get in early and make their mark on this exciting venture!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the &lt;strong&gt;Director of Community&lt;/strong&gt;, you will define the vision, strategy, and execution for the game&#39;s global player experience across Community Management and Customer Support. You will serve as the executive voice of the player, ensuring player needs, expectations, and sentiment are represented throughout development and live operations while building a trusted, long-lasting relationship between our players and the game team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a unique opportunity to build the Community and Customer Support function from the ground up. During development you will be highly hands-on, owning both strategy and execution while designing scalable systems, processes, and partnerships that can support millions of players as the game grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the long-term vision and strategy for Community Management and Customer Support as foundational pillars of the game&#39;s live service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the global Community strategy, building the Community function as the game progresses through announcement, closed beta, soft launch, and worldwide launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own a global player feedback loop that transforms community conversations, player research, customer support trends, and behavioral data into actionable insights for the development team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the community approach for major launches, updates, live moments, and player communications, ensuring clear and coordinated engagement across channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the global Customer Support strategy, including ticket operations, escalation processes, knowledge management, issue reporting, service quality, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define community health, engagement, sentiment, and feedback measures, using qualitative and quantitative insights to identify opportunities and emerging player needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong cross-functional partnerships across Marketing, Product, Development, Customer Support, Analytics, and other teams to ensure the player perspective informs planning and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead the Community and Customer Support disciplines as the game scales, establishing clear priorities, ways of working, and standards that enable the team to deliver effectively across a global player base&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience leading Community Management, Player Experience, Customer Support, or Live Operations for successful live-service games.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success building Community or Customer Support functions from the ground up, establishing scalable processes before large teams exist.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to balance strategic leadership with hands-on execution in fast-moving development environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing agencies, outsourcing partners, regional contractors, or external service providers to deliver global player experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence product strategy through player insights, community intelligence, and customer feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of live-service player expectations, community engagement, customer support operations, and trust-building strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with experience communicating effectively to both players and executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical mindset with experience using qualitative and quantitative data to drive strategic decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in ambiguity, wearing multiple hats, and helping establish entirely new functions during game development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for creating exceptional player experiences and building enduring relationships between players and developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working effectively across multiple time zones and global development teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining community strategy across multiple stages of a product lifecycle, with the ability to translate broader business and product goals into clear priorities and plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building effective player or customer feedback loops and translating community insights into actionable input for cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading through complex launches or live moments involving multiple stakeholders, changing priorities, and significant player communication needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment in sensitive or high-visibility community situations, balancing player needs, product context, business priorities, and reputational considerations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate complex or sensitive information clearly across player-facing channels and with stakeholders at different levels of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting mobile or free-to-play games and their communities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing community programs across multiple regions, languages, platforms, or player segments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on a major IP where partner alignment is key&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we create games for everyone - and want to ensure that the people behind our games reflect that! We are committed to creating a diverse, supportive work environment where everyone is treated with respect. We are committed to providing equal employment opportunities and welcome individuals from all backgrounds to join us &amp;amp; embrace the adventure!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For candidates in CA, CO, NJ, NY, and WA, the annual salary range is provided below. In addition to base pay, employees may be eligible for equity, bonuses, and a comprehensive benefits package, including healthcare benefits, retirement benefits, pet insurance, paid holidays, paid Scopely free days, and unlimited paid time off. Base pay offered may vary depending on job-related knowledge, skills, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;CA, CO, NJ, NY, and WA Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$139,400&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$172,200 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Scopely&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a leading video game and global interactive entertainment company, home to many of the world’s most beloved and enduring experiences, including two of the most successful mobile games of all-time “MONOPOLY GO!” and “Pokémon GO,” along with “Stumble Guys,” “Star Trek™ Fleet Command,” “MARVEL Strike Force,” “WWE Champions,” the Scrabble® franchise, “Yahtzee® With Buddies,” and many others. Across mobile, web, PC, and console, Scopely creates, develops, publishes, and live-operates one of the most diversified and award-winning portfolios in the games industry — bringing hundreds of millions of players together through a shared love of play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2011, Scopely is powered by its exceptional team — including thousands of world-class gamemakers around the globe, a distinctive tenet-driven culture, and its proprietary technology platform, Playgami. Together, these strengths have fueled Scopely’s position as the #1 mobile games company in the U.S. and #2 globally, generating more than $10 billion in lifetime revenue. Whether building global sensations like “MONOPOLY GO!” from the ground up, or expanding through strategic acquisitions, including the FoxNext, GSN, and Scopely Explore games businesses — Scopely consistently delivers experiences players love today and return to for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized multiple times as one of the &quot;100 Most Influential Companies in the World&quot; by TIME magazine and one of Fast Company&#39;s &quot;World&#39;s Most Innovative Companies&quot; and “Best Workplaces for Innovators,” Scopely believes that video games can be a force for good — creating meaningful connections, vibrant communities, and making life better through play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely has global operations and partners across four continents in more than a dozen countries worldwide. For more information, visit: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.scopely.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Candidates: Scopely will never request payment or financial information during the application or hiring process. Please apply only through our official &lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt; and verify that all Talent Partner communications come from an email address ending in @&lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;scopely.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Should you have any questions or encounter any fraudulent requests/emails/websites, please immediately contact recruiting@scopely.com. Our job applicant privacy policies are available here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/job-applicant-privacy-notice-for-ca-residents&quot;&gt;California Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/eea-and-uk-job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;EEA/UK Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employment at Scopely is based solely on a person&#39;s merit and qualifications. Scopely does not discriminate against any employee or applicant because of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), or any other basis protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;","departments":[{"id":4033443008,"name":"Publishing","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4036486008,"name":"Remote - California","location":null,"child_ids":[],"parent_id":4029782008}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/scopely/jobs/5363713008?gh_jid=5363713008","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":4329180008,"location":{"name":"ES - Barcelona, Spain"},"metadata":[{"id":4974618008,"name":"Worker Type","value":"Employee","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6354091008,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full Time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6354150008,"name":"Referral Bonus Payout Type","value":null,"value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6710077008,"name":"Work Arrangement","value":["Hybrid","Remote"],"value_type":"multi_select"},{"id":6752710008,"name":"Location","value":["Spain"],"value_type":"multi_select"},{"id":6755132008,"name":"Category","value":["Game Design and Production"],"value_type":"multi_select"}],"id":5363713008,"updated_at":"2026-09-02T07:52:02-04:00","requisition_id":"JR105116","title":"Director of Live Roadmap & Release Operations | MONOPOLY GO!","company_name":"Scopely","first_published":"2026-07-18T09:36:05-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Director of Live Roadmap &amp;amp; Release Operations&lt;/strong&gt; to join our &lt;strong&gt;MONOPOLY GO!&lt;/strong&gt; game team in Barcelona on a hybrid basis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MONOPOLY GO! is a global phenomenon and the biggest mobile game launch in history, captivating millions of players worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play every day—whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues or through our deep connections with our communities. We are a global team of game lovers developing, publishing, and innovating across the games industry, connecting millions of players around the world every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As &lt;strong&gt;Director of Live Roadmap &amp;amp; Release Operations&lt;/strong&gt;, you will own the operational health, integrity, and readiness of MONOPOLY GO!’s live roadmap and release ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead the systems, processes, and operating rhythms that turn product, content, events, promotions, tooling, and technical initiatives into coordinated and reliable live releases. This includes roadmap governance, dependency management, release readiness, risk assessment, deployment coordination, operational tooling, incident response, and post-release validation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the intersection of &lt;strong&gt;Production, Live Operations, Product, Engineering, and QA&lt;/strong&gt;. We are looking for someone who combines strong operational leadership with enough technical depth to work credibly with Engineering teams and improve the systems behind live delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The background could come from &lt;strong&gt;Live Operations, Production, Release Management, Technical Production, or Engineering Management&lt;/strong&gt;. What matters most is demonstrated experience operating close to live releases and production environments, coordinating complex cross-functional delivery, and improving the processes and technical systems that support execution at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You should be equally comfortable shaping long-term operating strategy, working through a complex dependency or release plan with delivery teams, partnering with engineers on tooling and automation, or stepping into a critical launch or incident to help drive resolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the operating health of the live roadmap, ensuring priorities, sequencing, dependencies, capacity, and release plans are realistic and executable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and evolve the end-to-end operating model for taking work from roadmap definition through development, validation, approval, deployment, monitoring, and post-release review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead release governance and readiness, including risk-based gates, clear ownership, go/no-go processes, escalation paths, rollback planning, and post-release validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate complex, high-frequency live releases across Product, Engineering, Live Operations, Production, QA, Content, and other partner teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify roadmap, technical, operational, and dependency risks early and drive clear mitigation and decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Engineering to improve deployment pipelines, configuration workflows, validation systems, observability, dashboards, automation, and operational tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate operational needs into clear technical requirements and help prioritize tooling and platform improvements that reduce manual work and release risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish metrics and reporting that provide visibility into roadmap health, release readiness, throughput, incidents, rework, operational load, and time to resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve production and release workflows by removing unnecessary handoffs, clarifying ownership, increasing automation, and creating sustainable operating standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Step into critical launches, incidents, or escalations when cross-functional coordination and rapid decision-making are required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead operational change across teams, helping new processes, tooling, and ways of working become embedded rather than simply introduced&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted partnerships across senior Product, Engineering, Production, QA, Data, and Live Operations leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor Producers, Release Managers, Engineering Managers, or other operational leaders involved in the live delivery ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience leading complex live operations, release management, technical production, engineering delivery, or a closely related function within a live-service environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience owning or influencing high-frequency releases across multiple teams, systems, dependencies, and concurrent workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operational judgment, with experience balancing delivery speed, technical risk, player experience, business priorities, and sustainable team execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency in software delivery and production environments, including deployment workflows, configuration management, validation, monitoring, rollback, and incident response&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering closely with Engineering teams on release tooling, automation, production systems, or workflow improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of roadmap planning, dependency management, release readiness, risk management, and operational governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience improving operating models, processes, tooling, or organizational ways of working across multiple teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to move comfortably between strategic planning and detailed execution, remaining close enough to delivery to identify issues and unblock teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management and cross-functional leadership, including the ability to align teams with different priorities without relying on direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading teams or developing leaders within Production, Live Operations, Release Management, Engineering, or adjacent functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication of technical, operational, and delivery risks to both technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;AI Capability &amp;amp; Readiness&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe AI can meaningfully transform how Live Operations and release organizations execute at scale. In this role, you’ll be expected to actively leverage AI-enabled tools to improve roadmap analysis, dependency mapping, release readiness, documentation, risk identification, incident response, production analytics, decision support, and workflow automation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value leaders who experiment thoughtfully with emerging AI technologies to reduce operational overhead, improve visibility and decision-making, increase release quality, and help teams move faster while maintaining strong standards of safety, accountability, and execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating a large-scale mobile free-to-play or other high-frequency live-service product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as an &lt;strong&gt;Engineering Manager with meaningful ownership of production delivery, releases, incidents, or Live Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a &lt;strong&gt;Technical Producer, Production Director, Release Director, Game Operations leader, or equivalent&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or operating release trains, deployment pipelines, feature-flag systems, configuration platforms, or production-control frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GameOps, LiveOps, developer productivity, release engineering, SRE, platform engineering, or adjacent technical operations functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building operational dashboards and release-health metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience introducing automated validation, change controls, release tooling, or post-deployment monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading globally distributed teams across multiple time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we create games for everyone - and want to ensure that the people behind our games reflect that! We are committed to creating a diverse, supportive work environment where everyone is treated with respect. We are committed to providing equal employment opportunities and welcome individuals from all backgrounds to join us &amp;amp; embrace the adventure!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Scopely&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a leading video game and global interactive entertainment company, home to many of the world’s most beloved and enduring experiences, including two of the most successful mobile games of all-time “MONOPOLY GO!” and “Pokémon GO,” along with “Stumble Guys,” “Star Trek™ Fleet Command,” “MARVEL Strike Force,” “WWE Champions,” the Scrabble® franchise, “Yahtzee® With Buddies,” and many others. Across mobile, web, PC, and console, Scopely creates, develops, publishes, and live-operates one of the most diversified and award-winning portfolios in the games industry — bringing hundreds of millions of players together through a shared love of play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2011, Scopely is powered by its exceptional team — including thousands of world-class gamemakers around the globe, a distinctive tenet-driven culture, and its proprietary technology platform, Playgami. Together, these strengths have fueled Scopely’s position as the #1 mobile games company in the U.S. and #2 globally, generating more than $10 billion in lifetime revenue. Whether building global sensations like “MONOPOLY GO!” from the ground up, or expanding through strategic acquisitions, including the FoxNext, GSN, and Scopely Explore games businesses — Scopely consistently delivers experiences players love today and return to for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized multiple times as one of the &quot;100 Most Influential Companies in the World&quot; by TIME magazine and one of Fast Company&#39;s &quot;World&#39;s Most Innovative Companies&quot; and “Best Workplaces for Innovators,” Scopely believes that video games can be a force for good — creating meaningful connections, vibrant communities, and making life better through play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely has global operations and partners across four continents in more than a dozen countries worldwide. For more information, visit: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.scopely.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Candidates: Scopely will never request payment or financial information during the application or hiring process. Please apply only through our official &lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt; and verify that all Talent Partner communications come from an email address ending in @&lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;scopely.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Should you have any questions or encounter any fraudulent requests/emails/websites, please immediately contact recruiting@scopely.com. Our job applicant privacy policies are available here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/job-applicant-privacy-notice-for-ca-residents&quot;&gt;California Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/eea-and-uk-job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;EEA/UK Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employment at Scopely is based solely on a person&#39;s merit and qualifications. Scopely does not discriminate against any employee or applicant because of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), or any other basis protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;","departments":[{"id":4033439008,"name":"MonopolyGo","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4036218008,"name":"London","location":null,"child_ids":[],"parent_id":4036217008}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/scopely/jobs/5021595008?gh_jid=5021595008","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":4381206008,"location":{"name":"JP - Tokyo, Japan"},"metadata":[{"id":4974618008,"name":"Worker Type","value":"Employee","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6354091008,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full Time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6354150008,"name":"Referral Bonus Payout Type","value":null,"value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6710077008,"name":"Work Arrangement","value":["Hybrid"],"value_type":"multi_select"},{"id":6752710008,"name":"Location","value":["Japan"],"value_type":"multi_select"},{"id":6755132008,"name":"Category","value":["Marketing"],"value_type":"multi_select"}],"id":5021595008,"updated_at":"2026-08-18T01:02:03-04:00","requisition_id":"JR105537","title":"Director of Marketing - Monster Hunter Now","company_name":"Scopely","first_published":"2025-12-12T03:59:59-05:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;Scopely Explore (formerly known as Niantic) is looking for a Marketing Director to lead the go-to-market strategy and execution of marketing communication for Monster Hunter Now. The ideal candidate possesses a genuine passion for the product, and can handle multiple responsibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will lead a team of skilled, savvy, and hardworking marketers to build impactful consumer touchpoints across user acquisition, social media, community engagement, and IRL events. You will also work with executives, cross-functional teammates, and external business partners. Most importantly, you’ll have a lot of fun while contributing to Scopely Explore&#39;s mission of inspiring people to explore the world together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As this is a global product, you will need to collaborate with teammates from around the world to ensure consistency and accuracy across all regions for any marketing initiative.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the Monster Hunter Now marketing team by demonstrating in-depth knowledge of mobile game/app marketing tactics, user acquisition, engagement and retention, as well as effective general marketing practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Together with the team, solidify product positioning, author key messaging, and help develop marketing campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and successfully implement go-to-market, engagement &amp;amp; retention strategies in close coordination with fellow marketing colleagues and cross-functional partners such as Product Management, Business Development, Operations, Communications, and Legal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and manage the marketing budget for Monster Hunter Now. Conduct return on investment analyses on all campaigns and apply takeaways to future programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional team members and external partners to cultivate strong working relationships with project team members, including regular and reliable attendance and participation in meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and evolve existing workflows, proactively identifying opportunities to build AI-driven solutions and automation to improve productivity, eliminate repetitive tasks, reduce errors and increase overall quality of work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively get involved in initiatives to promote AI solutions and be at the forefront of thought leadership for AI-driven solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nurture relationships with key executives in Japan and US, and drive global alignment on major marketing initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the team in a multi-cultural environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Required in-office attendance 3 days a week on Tuesdays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;14+ years of relevant marketing experience in areas including: product positioning strategies that factor in market dynamics and user insights, paid media campaign strategy and management including creative development, agency selection, media planning &amp;amp; buying, campaign tracking, and optimization, social media marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on a highly cross-functional with the ability to coordinate dynamic projects with internal and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding verbal and written communication skills in English and Japanese, with experience in developing and delivering executive-level presentations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding and passion for Scopely Explore’s mission and values.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a fast-paced hybrid environment. Handle stress appropriately. Solve practical problems and adapt to dynamic situations with little notice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Scopely&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a leading video game and global interactive entertainment company, home to many of the world’s most beloved and enduring experiences, including two of the most successful mobile games of all-time “MONOPOLY GO!” and “Pokémon GO,” along with “Stumble Guys,” “Star Trek™ Fleet Command,” “MARVEL Strike Force,” “WWE Champions,” the Scrabble® franchise, “Yahtzee® With Buddies,” and many others. Across mobile, web, PC, and console, Scopely creates, develops, publishes, and live-operates one of the most diversified and award-winning portfolios in the games industry — bringing hundreds of millions of players together through a shared love of play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2011, Scopely is powered by its exceptional team — including thousands of world-class gamemakers around the globe, a distinctive tenet-driven culture, and its proprietary technology platform, Playgami. Together, these strengths have fueled Scopely’s position as the #1 mobile games company in the U.S. and #2 globally, generating more than $10 billion in lifetime revenue. Whether building global sensations like “MONOPOLY GO!” from the ground up, or expanding through strategic acquisitions, including the FoxNext, GSN, and Scopely Explore games businesses — Scopely consistently delivers experiences players love today and return to for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized multiple times as one of the &quot;100 Most Influential Companies in the World&quot; by TIME magazine and one of Fast Company&#39;s &quot;World&#39;s Most Innovative Companies&quot; and “Best Workplaces for Innovators,” Scopely believes that video games can be a force for good — creating meaningful connections, vibrant communities, and making life better through play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely has global operations and partners across four continents in more than a dozen countries worldwide. For more information, visit: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.scopely.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
