t":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Scopely is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Lead&amp;nbsp;3D Artist&lt;/strong&gt; to join the &lt;strong&gt;MONOPOLY GO!&lt;/strong&gt; team in Barcelona on a hybrid basis.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and strive to inspire play every day—whether through our collaborative work environment or our connection with the global communities who enjoy our games. We are a diverse team of passionate creators developing, publishing, and innovating within the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world every day.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;MONOPOLY GO! is a global phenomenon and the biggest mobile game launch in history, captivating millions of players worldwide.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and uphold the 3D vision for each season, in partnership with the Art Director, Principal Artist, and Content Leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the bar for quality, technical craft, and AI-assisted workflows, and hold the whole team to it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifying where Ai assisted workflows create meaningful production value, establishing standards for quality and consistency, and turning successful experimentation into repeatable practices the wider team can adopt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and continuously improve the 3D pipeline&#39;s standards and guideline documentation, partnering with Technical Art on implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and mentor the discipline, owning performance reviews, goal-setting, and team health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in hiring to make sure new hires are the right fit, and champion the team&#39;s culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the primary point of contact and voice for 3D, coordinating the discipline&#39;s work with the rest of production, from planning through delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years experience as a 3D artist working in games, including 3+ years leading, mentoring, and setting the artistic bar for a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience developing, scaling, and driving adoption of AI-assisted creative workflows, with the judgment to evaluate their impact on quality, consistency, efficiency, and downstream production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record shipping multiple mobile titles in casual/whimsical art styles, partnering across Design, Engineering, and outsourcing to deliver high-quality content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing, standardizing, or automating 3D production pipelines, including AI/ML-driven tooling, backed by expert proficiency across the toolset (Maya/Blender/3ds Max, Substance, Unity)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Positive attitude and the ability to give and receive objective feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing or supporting multiple outsourcing partners while holding their output to a consistent quality standard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating the brand guidelines and approval pipeline of at least one externally-licensed IP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for playing and making games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
