"content":"&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Accounting Associate &lt;/strong&gt;to join our fast-growing Accounting organization in our Barcelona offices. This person will assist in the day-to-day operations of the Accounting team as well as own and manage Accounting initiatives and projects in perpetuity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage monthly and quarterly lease accounting close activities, including preparation and posting of lease amortization journal entries for operating and finance leases under U.S. GAAP and IFRS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and review monthly and quarterly lease-related account reconciliations and roll-forwards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review new lease contracts, amendments, renewals, and terminations to determine appropriate accounting treatment under ASC 842 and IFRS 16.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the maintenance and administration of lease accounting software, including data inputs, system-generated calculations, reporting, and controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support quarterly and annual financial statement disclosures related to leases under U.S. GAAP and IFRS. Analyze variances in lease-related balance sheet and income statement accounts and provide clear explanations to management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support process improvements and enhancements to lease accounting workflows and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage fixed asset accounting activities, if assigned, including preparing and maintaining fixed asset roll-forwards and supporting related financial statement disclosures, management reporting, and audit requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support additional general ledger accounting areas as business needs evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate effectively with various teams, subsidiaries, and external auditors to address queries and provide necessary information during audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What we are looking for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 4 years’ experience with lease accounting under ASC 842 and IFRS 16&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 4 years’ experience in general ledger accounting, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or associate&#39;s degree in accounting, or in a related specialization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of U.S. GAAP and IFRS accounting principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, constantly changing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in working in an international company over multiple locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated history of process improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience working with Oracle will be an advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communications skills in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced user of Microsoft Excel and other MS packages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
