nguage":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;We are looking for Sr CRM Manager, for our game Star Trek Fleet Command&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;to join our team in Barcelona.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play every day - whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing and innovating the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Will You Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This person owns the end-to-end communication ecosystem—strategy, calendar, messaging, and creative direction—ensuring a cohesive and player-first narrative across all CRM touchpoints. They partner closely with Product, Live Ops, and Marketing to influence what is built and when, so that player journeys are fully supported and optimized for engagement, retention, and LTV.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your key responsibilities will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Player Communication Strategy&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the CRM and lifecycle communication calendar, aligning all messaging with live ops events, feature releases, and key player moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and evolve lifecycle strategies across key segments (new, active, lapsing, VIP, and conversion-focused cohorts)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate product and live ops plans into clear, actionable communication strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the single source of truth for all outbound player messaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Creative &amp;amp; Messaging Leadership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead development of messaging across push, email, in-game surfaces, and other CRM channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and/or guide high-quality, performance-driven copy tailored to player motivations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with design to develop compelling creative that reinforces campaign goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure consistency in brand voice, tone, and player-first communication standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a library of high-performing templates, subject lines, and creative assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Live Ops &amp;amp; Product Influence&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent CRM in sprint planning and live ops reviews, advocating for lifecycle needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence feature design (e.g., messaging surfaces, onboarding flows, opt-ins) to improve reach and effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Live Ops to align event timing, offers, and promotions with the communication strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and prioritize data and targeting requirements to enable personalization and segmentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Campaign Execution &amp;amp; Experimentation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brief Marketing Operations on campaign builds, including targeting, timing, creative, and success metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and approve campaigns prior to launch to ensure quality and alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with CRM Analytics to design and prioritize experiments (A/B tests, holdouts, journey optimization)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze campaign performance and translate insights into actionable improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Game &amp;amp; Community Immersion&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively play Star Trek Fleet Command to maintain a strong understanding of the player experience and economy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay informed on community sentiment, feedback, and trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in stand-ups, design reviews, and live ops planning to remain closely aligned with the game team&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CROSS-FUNCTIONAL IMPACT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is the primary bridge between the central CRM function and the game team. The CRM / Lifecycle Lead owns direct-to-player campaigns end-to-end and ensures alignment across Social, Community, and Player Experience (Px) channels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While supported by a Marketing Operations Manager and CRM Analyst, this role is expected to operate as a senior individual contributor with strong hands-on capabilities in campaign execution, segmentation, and experimentation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in CRM, lifecycle marketing, product marketing, or growth roles with hands-on channel execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in midcore mobile games (professional and/or deeply engaged player)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong creative instincts with the ability to write compelling, high-performing copy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing editorial or communication calendars in live service environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working within sprint-based development and influencing product decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with CRM platforms (e.g., Braze, Iterable) and lifecycle orchestration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical mindset with experience using data to inform strategy and optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional communication and stakeholder management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Scopely&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a leading video game and global interactive entertainment company, home to many of the world’s most beloved and enduring experiences, including two of the most successful mobile games of all-time “MONOPOLY GO!” and “Pokémon GO,” along with “Stumble Guys,” “Star Trek™ Fleet Command,” “MARVEL Strike Force,” “WWE Champions,” the Scrabble® franchise, “Yahtzee® With Buddies,” and many others. Across mobile, web, PC, and console, Scopely creates, develops, publishes, and live-operates one of the most diversified and award-winning portfolios in the games industry — bringing hundreds of millions of players together through a shared love of play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2011, Scopely is powered by its exceptional team — including thousands of world-class gamemakers around the globe, a distinctive tenet-driven culture, and its proprietary technology platform, Playgami. Together, these strengths have fueled Scopely’s position as the #1 mobile games company in the U.S. and #2 globally, generating more than $10 billion in lifetime revenue. Whether building global sensations like “MONOPOLY GO!” from the ground up, or expanding through strategic acquisitions, including the FoxNext, GSN, and Scopely Explore games businesses — Scopely consistently delivers experiences players love today and return to for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized multiple times as one of the &quot;100 Most Influential Companies in the World&quot; by TIME magazine and one of Fast Company&#39;s &quot;World&#39;s Most Innovative Companies&quot; and “Best Workplaces for Innovators,” Scopely believes that video games can be a force for good — creating meaningful connections, vibrant communities, and making life better through play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely has global operations and partners across four continents in more than a dozen countries worldwide. For more information, visit: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.scopely.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Candidates: Scopely will never request payment or financial information during the application or hiring process. Please apply only through our official &lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt; and verify that all Talent Partner communications come from an email address ending in @&lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;scopely.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Should you have any questions or encounter any fraudulent requests/emails/websites, please immediately contact recruiting@scopely.com. Our job applicant privacy policies are available here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/job-applicant-privacy-notice-for-ca-residents&quot;&gt;California Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/eea-and-uk-job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;EEA/UK Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employment at Scopely is based solely on a person&#39;s merit and qualifications. Scopely does not discriminate against any employee or applicant because of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), or any other basis protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;","departments":[{"id":4033443008,"name":"Publishing","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4036543008,"name":"Barcelona","location":null,"child_ids":[],"parent_id":4036454008}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/scopely/jobs/5234167008?gh_jid=5234167008","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":4481444008,"location":{"name":"US - San Francisco, United States"},"metadata":[{"id":4974618008,"name":"Worker Type","value":"Employee","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6354091008,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full Time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6354150008,"name":"Referral Bonus Payout Type","value":null,"value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6710077008,"name":"Work Arrangement","value":null,"value_type":"multi_select"},{"id":6752710008,"name":"Location","value":["United States"],"value_type":"multi_select"},{"id":6755132008,"name":"Category","value":null,"value_type":"multi_select"}],"id":5234167008,"updated_at":"2026-08-18T16:52:52-04:00","requisition_id":"JR106278","title":"Senior Data Scientist, Marketing","company_name":"Scopely","first_published":"2026-06-03T21:28:31-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a global gaming company whose mission is to inspire play every day. Scopely Explore (a division of Scopely)’s mission is to inspire people to explore the world together. We build products that inspire exercise, exploration, and social in-person interaction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a quantitatively adept and business-minded &lt;strong&gt;Senior Data Scientist, Marketing&lt;/strong&gt;, to support our global marketing organization. You will operate at the intersection of &lt;strong&gt;data science&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;deep marketing domain expertise&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;AI proficiency&lt;/strong&gt;. In this role, you will help develop measurement frameworks, analytical models(e.g Marketing Mix Modeling), and scalable reporting solutions that inform user acquisition, brand investment, CRM efforts, and long-term player growth. You will also utilize AI-augmented workflows to accelerate the end-to-end data science lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for someone who combines strong technical skills with intellectual curiosity, a forward-thinking perspective on how AI will transform data science workflows, and a desire to understand how marketing investments translate into long-term player value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;User Acquisition (UA)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to and own the Marketing Mix Modeling (MMM) and other aggregate measurement approaches to evaluate cross-channel and upper-funnel impact (e.g. brand) where deterministic attribution is limited.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain robust ETL pipelines that ingest, transform, and validate UA data from ad networks, MMPs, and internal systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and refine predictive LTV (pLTV) models to enable faster optimization of UA campaigns based on early user signals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore, develop, and refine AI-based systems that are able to answer common data inquiries from stakeholders, as well as quickly diagnose data pipeline issues, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support testing frameworks (e.g., geo experiments, holdouts, incrementality tests) to evaluate campaign effectiveness in privacy-constrained environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance and UA teams to align on forecasting methodologies and investment strategies driven by pLTV and payback periods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct Marketing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain reliable datasets and ETL workflows that ingest and transform marketing data from ad platforms, CRM systems, social channels, and internal data sources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support measurement and optimization of direct marketing channels including email, push notifications, in-app messaging, and other CRM/lifecycle campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Marketing stakeholders to provide actionable insights on targeting, segmentation, messaging effectiveness, and channel strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytics Infrastructure &amp;amp; Workflow Efficiency&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to scalable dashboards and standardized reporting that enable self-serve marketing analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to automate recurring reporting and insight generation for marketing stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage modern AI/ML tools (e.g., automated modeling workflows, AI coding assistants) to improve analysis speed, code quality, and documentation and bridge the gap between technical AI-driven insights and business stakeholders to ensure output is accurate and aligned with complex business logic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure data quality, documentation, and consistency across marketing data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to responsible and thoughtful adoption of AI-powered analytics tools to ensure maintainability and long-term knowledge sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4-8 years of experience in data science, marketing analytics, or a related quantitative role (gaming, mobile, or digital consumer experience preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated proficiency in integrating AI agentic tools to accelerate end-to-end data science workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in user acquisition measurement and attribution with exposure to Marketing Mix Modeling or other aggregate-level measurement frameworks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of full marketing funnel, including brand/awareness, social, UA, and direct marketing channels (e.g., email, push, CRM).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with core performance metrics such as CAC, ROAS, retention, engagement, and LTV.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with marketing data from ad platforms, CRM systems, or aggregate reporting environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in SQL and experience using Python (or similar) for analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with large datasets in a cloud data warehouse (e.g., BigQuery) and building dashboards in BI tools (e.g., Looker).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, communication, and stakeholder management skills in a cross-functional environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Plus If…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting brand or upper-funnel marketing measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with lifecycle marketing analytics, segmentation modeling, or propensity modeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building marketing data pipelines using Airflow, Composer, or similar orchestration tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with global marketing teams across multiple regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For candidates in CA, CO, NJ, NY, and WA, the annual salary range is provided below. In addition to base pay, employees may be eligible for equity, bonuses, and a comprehensive benefits package, including healthcare benefits, retirement benefits, pet insurance, paid holidays, paid Scopely free days, and unlimited paid time off. Base pay offered may vary depending on job-related knowledge, skills, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;CA, CO, NJ, NY, and WA Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$17,100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$253,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Scopely&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a leading video game and global interactive entertainment company, home to many of the world’s most beloved and enduring experiences, including two of the most successful mobile games of all-time “MONOPOLY GO!” and “Pokémon GO,” along with “Stumble Guys,” “Star Trek™ Fleet Command,” “MARVEL Strike Force,” “WWE Champions,” the Scrabble® franchise, “Yahtzee® With Buddies,” and many others. Across mobile, web, PC, and console, Scopely creates, develops, publishes, and live-operates one of the most diversified and award-winning portfolios in the games industry — bringing hundreds of millions of players together through a shared love of play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2011, Scopely is powered by its exceptional team — including thousands of world-class gamemakers around the globe, a distinctive tenet-driven culture, and its proprietary technology platform, Playgami. Together, these strengths have fueled Scopely’s position as the #1 mobile games company in the U.S. and #2 globally, generating more than $10 billion in lifetime revenue. Whether building global sensations like “MONOPOLY GO!” from the ground up, or expanding through strategic acquisitions, including the FoxNext, GSN, and Scopely Explore games businesses — Scopely consistently delivers experiences players love today and return to for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized multiple times as one of the &quot;100 Most Influential Companies in the World&quot; by TIME magazine and one of Fast Company&#39;s &quot;World&#39;s Most Innovative Companies&quot; and “Best Workplaces for Innovators,” Scopely believes that video games can be a force for good — creating meaningful connections, vibrant communities, and making life better through play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely has global operations and partners across four continents in more than a dozen countries worldwide. For more information, visit: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.scopely.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Candidates: Scopely will never request payment or financial information during the application or hiring process. Please apply only through our official &lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt; and verify that all Talent Partner communications come from an email address ending in @&lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;scopely.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Should you have any questions or encounter any fraudulent requests/emails/websites, please immediately contact recruiting@scopely.com. Our job applicant privacy policies are available here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/job-applicant-privacy-notice-for-ca-residents&quot;&gt;California Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/eea-and-uk-job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;EEA/UK Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employment at Scopely is based solely on a person&#39;s merit and qualifications. Scopely does not discriminate against any employee or applicant because of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), or any other basis protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;","departments":[{"id":4069345008,"name":"Scopely Explore","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4046126008,"name":"San Francisco - Bay 3","location":null,"child_ids":[],"parent_id":4046122008}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/scopely/jobs/5123217008?gh_jid=5123217008","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":4429449008,"location":{"name":"ES - Barcelona, Spain"},"metadata":[{"id":4974618008,"name":"Worker Type","value":"Employee","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6354091008,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full Time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6354150008,"name":"Referral Bonus Payout Type","value":null,"value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6710077008,"name":"Work Arrangement","value":null,"value_type":"multi_select"},{"id":6752710008,"name":"Location","value":["Spain"],"value_type":"multi_select"},{"id":6755132008,"name":"Category","value":["Marketing"],"value_type":"multi_select"}],"id":5123217008,"updated_at":"2026-08-05T06:35:33-04:00","requisition_id":"JR105829","title":"Senior Director, Marketing – New Game Launch","company_name":"Scopely","first_published":"2026-02-20T05:14:57-05:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a&amp;nbsp;Senior Director, Marketing to lead marketing across the Scrabble franchise, including Scrabble Go and an exciting new unannounced mobile title, based in Barcelona on a hybrid basis (2 days per week in office).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a rare opportunity for a marketing leader who wants to shape both the future of an iconic live game and the launch of something entirely new. You will define the go-to-market strategy for a new title from the ground up, while also driving the long-term growth strategy for one of mobile gaming’s most recognizable franchises.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a strategic, highly analytical, and creatively ambitious leader who can operate as the Head of Marketing for the franchise—bringing together product marketing, community, creator, lifecycle, creative, and performance marketing into one clear plan for growth. You’ll partner closely with game teams, central marketing functions, and executive stakeholders to build campaigns, shape positioning, guide launch strategy, and create meaningful player demand before, during, and after launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play every day—whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers developing, publishing, and innovating in the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the marketing vision and strategy for the Scrabble franchise, spanning both Scrabble Go and a new unannounced mobile title&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the global go-to-market strategy for a new game launch, from audience definition and market opportunity to positioning, campaign planning, launch readiness, and post-launch momentum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define compelling product positioning, messaging, and value propositions that translate gameplay features into clear, differentiated player-facing stories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop integrated marketing strategies across the full player funnel, driving acquisition, activation, retention, advocacy, and long-term franchise growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape creative strategy in partnership with internal and external creative teams, and guide the development of high-performing marketing across UA, social, influencer, community, CRM, and lifecycle channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute 360 marketing campaigns informed by player insights, market research, testing, competitive analysis, and performance data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product, Performance Marketing, Creative, Analytics, CRM, and Licensors to align strategy and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the key marketing partner to game leadership, influencing how each title is brought to market and ensuring the strongest player benefits and differentiators are reflected in both the product and its marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion the voice of the player by bringing customer needs, behaviors, pain points, and feedback into product strategy, roadmap conversations, and feature prioritization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop launch narratives, campaign frameworks, and executive-ready communication materials that align stakeholders and drive decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and nurture community and creator programs that generate excitement ahead of launch, deepen player engagement, and strengthen long-term franchise affinity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with licensors and external partners, ensuring alignment across brand, product, and launch priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As the franchise grows, build and lead a high-performing marketing team with the ability to execute, learn, and adapt as the business evolves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience in product marketing, game marketing, growth marketing, or related functions, with meaningful time spent leading strategy for live and/or launching games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience bringing games or digital products to market successfully, ideally including ownership of major launch or GTM initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong track record of developing differentiated positioning, messaging, and go-to-market strategies that deliver business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across acquisition, activation, retention, community, creator, and lifecycle marketing to drive growth across the full player journey&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep fluency in game and marketing KPIs, with the ability to translate data, research, and competitive insight into clear strategic action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong creative instincts and experience shaping campaigns, narratives, and player-facing marketing that break through in a crowded market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate at both strategic and hands-on levels: setting vision, solving problems, and driving execution through cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to align teams and influence senior leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with external agencies, licensors, creators, or other third-party partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative leadership style and a reputation for building trust, energy, and alignment across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine passion for games and a strong instinct for what makes players engage, stay, and advocate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in mobile gaming, especially in casual games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the mobile user acquisition and performance marketing landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience adapting global marketing strategies and campaigns across different markets and audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience helping build or scale marketing teams in high-growth environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Information&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role is based in Barcelona, Spain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid schedule: 2 days per week in office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are open to hiring at the Director or Senior Director level depending on experience and scope alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Scopely&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a leading video game and global interactive entertainment company, home to many of the world’s most beloved and enduring experiences, including two of the most successful mobile games of all-time “MONOPOLY GO!” and “Pokémon GO,” along with “Stumble Guys,” “Star Trek™ Fleet Command,” “MARVEL Strike Force,” “WWE Champions,” the Scrabble® franchise, “Yahtzee® With Buddies,” and many others. Across mobile, web, PC, and console, Scopely creates, develops, publishes, and live-operates one of the most diversified and award-winning portfolios in the games industry — bringing hundreds of millions of players together through a shared love of play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2011, Scopely is powered by its exceptional team — including thousands of world-class gamemakers around the globe, a distinctive tenet-driven culture, and its proprietary technology platform, Playgami. Together, these strengths have fueled Scopely’s position as the #1 mobile games company in the U.S. and #2 globally, generating more than $10 billion in lifetime revenue. Whether building global sensations like “MONOPOLY GO!” from the ground up, or expanding through strategic acquisitions, including the FoxNext, GSN, and Scopely Explore games businesses — Scopely consistently delivers experiences players love today and return to for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized multiple times as one of the &quot;100 Most Influential Companies in the World&quot; by TIME magazine and one of Fast Company&#39;s &quot;World&#39;s Most Innovative Companies&quot; and “Best Workplaces for Innovators,” Scopely believes that video games can be a force for good — creating meaningful connections, vibrant communities, and making life better through play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely has global operations and partners across four continents in more than a dozen countries worldwide. For more information, visit: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.scopely.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Candidates: Scopely will never request payment or financial information during the application or hiring process. Please apply only through our official &lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt; and verify that all Talent Partner communications come from an email address ending in @&lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;scopely.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
