-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Producer&lt;/strong&gt; to join our WWE Champions team in the US or Canada on a remote basis.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play every day - whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing and innovating the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WWE Champions&lt;/strong&gt; is our ultimate and unique RPG puzzle match game featuring WWE superstars and legends across mobile and PC platforms. WWE Champions is the most downloaded WWE game to date, with a highly engaged and passionate community - who will remain undefeated?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced Senior Producer to help drive execution, accountability, and operational excellence across WWE Champions. This role is ideal for someone who thrives in highly complex live-service environments and enjoys bringing structure, predictability, and clarity to fast-moving teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reports to the Executive Producer and will play a key role in shaping how WWE Champions delivers value to players while operating as a healthy, sustainable live service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own production oversight for a portfolio of features, LiveOps initiatives, and strategic roadmap investments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate product strategy into actionable plans, milestones, dependencies, and release schedules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive execution across multiple concurrent workstreams, ensuring teams remain aligned, accountable, and focused on delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and manage risks, blockers, dependencies, and scope changes while providing clear mitigation plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate release planning, launch readiness, and cross-functional coordination across Product, Design, Engineering, QA, Analytics, and Live Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with studio leadership to improve operational efficiency, delivery predictability, and production best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide clear communication, status reporting, delivery forecasts, and risk assessments to stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of production experience in games, software, or live-service products, including 3+ years in a Senior Producer or equivalent leadership role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record delivering complex features from concept through launch on a live-service product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing cross-functional teams across multiple disciplines, stakeholders, and time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in planning, dependency management, risk management, release planning, and operational execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of LiveOps, monetization systems, player engagement, and live-service development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced experience with Jira and production workflows, including reporting, process improvement, and project tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, stakeholder management, and organizational skills, with the ability to drive alignment and accountability across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in fast-paced environments, managing ambiguity, and balancing short-term business priorities with long-term team health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with collection RPGs, gacha systems, progression economies, or wrestling games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with distributed internal and external development teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing production within a legacy codebase or mature live-service product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
