ation_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer (Unity)&lt;/strong&gt; to join our WWE Champions&amp;nbsp; team in Bangalore on a hybrid basis!&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;br&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play, every day - whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues, or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing and innovating the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;WWE Champions is our ultimate and unique RPG puzzle match game featuring WWE superstars and legends across mobile and PC platforms.&amp;nbsp; WWE Champions is the most downloaded WWE game to date, with a highly engaged and passionate community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Software Engineer, you will play a key role in developing and maintaining the game’s Unity client across a large live-service mobile game codebase. You will contribute to high-impact initiatives spanning gameplay systems, live-ops features, client infrastructure, performance, build reliability, platform integrations, and maintainability. This role is ideal for an engineer who combines strong technical execution with sound architectural judgment in a complex production environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain major client systems across gameplay, UI, live events, progression, offers, social features, and platform services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the architecture of a large Unity/C# codebase with an emphasis on modularity, testability, performance, and long-term maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and support data-driven and live-ops systems, including event configuration, feature flags, localization, and content delivered through structured data pipelines such as FlatBuffers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with design, product, QA, analytics, economy, backend, and live-ops stakeholders to deliver scalable client solutions aligned with roadmap and operational needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve engineering effectiveness through strong coding practices, tooling, CI/build processes, code reviews, debugging workflows, and technical documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and resolve production issues across mobile client systems, platform integrations, monetization flows, and live event features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior and mid-level engineers, contribute to team technical decisions, and help raise the overall quality bar for the engineering organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Technical Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional software engineering experience, including experience on production game clients or similarly complex interactive applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in C# and object-oriented software design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience with Unity in production environments, ideally on mobile live-service titles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and maintaining client systems for gameplay, UI, event systems, or data-driven feature development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mobile platform considerations for iOS and Android, including integrations, performance tuning, memory management, and release readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of client-side data pipelines, remote content/configuration, serialization, and schema-driven systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with build automation, CI/CD workflows, and release pipelines for mobile games.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong debugging and profiling skills across runtime behavior, performance, memory, and production stability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with testing strategies and quality practices in medium to large codebases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional and Game-Specific Knowledge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with live-service game development, including progression systems, offers/monetization, event systems, social features, and analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with backend and live-ops teams to support content updates and feature rollouts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to make thoughtful technical tradeoffs in a content-heavy, operationally active game environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working across teams and contributing to initiatives with multiple dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Soft Skills &amp;amp; Education&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and collaboration skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated mentorship and knowledge-sharing ability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ownership, sound judgment, and a practical approach to solving complex technical problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for games and for building stable, maintainable systems that support great player experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
